---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = "Common Scams in China & How to Avoid Them";
const description = "Don't let scammers ruin your China trip. Here are the most common tourist scams in China and exactly how to avoid them.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="zh">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-8 not-prose">
      <a href="/zh/tips/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-700 transition no-underline group">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
        </svg>
        Back to Tips
      </a>
    </nav>
    <!-- Header -->
  <header class="mb-12">
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">🛡️ 中国旅游小贴士</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">
      Common Scams in China<br class="hidden md:block" />& How to Avoid Them
    </h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">不要让骗子毁了你的旅行。以下是需要注意的事项。</p>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
      <span>📅 最后更新日期：2026年6月</span>
      <span>⏱️ 阅读6分钟</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- Quick Answer Box -->
  <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-red-50 to-orange-50 border-l-4 border-red-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-red-900 mb-4">⏱️ 阅读4分钟</h2>
    <p class="text-lg text-red-800 leading-relaxed">
      <strong>绝大多数中国人都是诚实和乐于助人的。</strong> But like everywhere with tourism, some target tourists. The scams here target your <strong>信任和友善</strong>, not your fear. If a stranger is <em>太</em> friendly and wants to take you somewhere — that's your red flag.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Table of Contents -->
  <nav class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">📋 在本指南中</h3>
    <ul class="space-y-3">
      <li><a href="#tea-house" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🍵 1.茶馆或艺术工作室邀请函</a></li>
      <li><a href="#fake-taxi" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🚕 2.假冒出租车和仪表</a></li>
      <li><a href="#free-gift" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🎁 3.“免费赠品”然后付款</a></li>
      <li><a href="#shop-tour" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🛍️ 4.“我的朋友有商店”之旅</a></li>
      <li><a href="#what-to-do" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🆘 如果发生什么事该怎么办</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <!-- Main Content -->
  <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
      Let me start by saying this honestly: <strong>绝大多数中国人诚实、热情，会不遗余力地帮助外国游客。</strong>
    </p>

    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-12">
      But like every country with tourism, some people target tourists. The scams here target your <strong>trust and friendliness</strong>, not your fear. Here's what to watch for.
    </p>

    <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

    <!-- Scam 1 -->
    <h2 id="tea-house" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
      <span class="text-4xl">🍵</span> 1. The Tea House or Art Studio Invitation
    </h2>

    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-900 mb-3">⚠️ 运作原理</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-800 leading-relaxed">
        A friendly young person approaches you near a major landmark. They say they're a student practicing English, or an art student who wants to show you a "traditional ceremony." After chatting, they take you to a nearby tea house or "studio." Staff serve you tea or demonstrate calligraphy, then hand you a bill for <strong>数百或数千元人民币</strong> — and the atmosphere turns suddenly unfriendly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-900 mb-3">✅ 如何避免</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-800">
        <li>礼貌但坚定：“对不起，我不感兴趣”——然后走开</li>
        <li>即使它们看起来是真实的，也不要跟着陌生人去第二个地方</li>
        <li>如果你最终陷入其中，请报警（110）——这些地方依赖恐吓，而不是法律权威</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-400 p-5 rounded-r-xl mb-12 not-prose">
      <p class="text-blue-900 font-semibold mb-2">💡 本地提示</p>
      <p class="text-blue-800 leading-relaxed">
        Genuine students looking to practice English will only chat with you casually on the spot. They won't drag you off to any unfamiliar locations, nor will they ask for your contact information to keep in touch. That rarely happens naturally. <strong>如果有人接近你并想成为你的朋友，十有八九，这是一种安排。</strong>
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

    <!-- Scam 2 -->
    <h2 id="fake-taxi" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
      <span class="text-4xl">🚕</span> 2. Fake Taxis and Rigged Meters
    </h2>

    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-900 mb-3">⚠️ How It Works</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-800 leading-relaxed">
        At airports and train stations, a driver approaches you offering a ride. These unlicensed private vehicles, commonly known as "black cabs", often disguise themselves as taxis. Drivers usually charge a flat per-person rate, which is far higher than the fares of official licensed cars. What's worse, riding them comes with no safety guarantees.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-800 leading-relaxed mt-3">
        <strong>常见的地方：</strong> Major airports, high-speed rail stations
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-900 mb-3">✅ How to Avoid It</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-800">
        <li><strong>使用滴滴</strong> (China's Uber equivalent) — prices are shown upfront, tracked, and you can share your ride with friends</li>
        <li>If you must take a taxi, <strong>使用官方出租车排队</strong> at the airport — ignore drivers waiting outside</li>
        <li>如果司机拒绝使用计价器或报出的价格似乎太高，请下车</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

    <!-- Scam 3 -->
    <h2 id="free-gift" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
      <span class="text-4xl">🎁</span> 3. The "Free Gift" Then Payment
    </h2>

    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-900 mb-3">⚠️ How It Works</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-800 leading-relaxed">
        Someone offers you a "free" gift — a bracelet, a calligraphy scroll with your name, a Buddhist charm. The moment you accept it or let them put it on you, they demand payment. The "monk blessing" scam is the most common version of this.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-800 leading-relaxed mt-3">
        <strong>Where it's common:</strong> Temples outside, tourist markets, near train stations
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-900 mb-3">✅ How to Avoid It</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-800">
        <li>不要接受街上陌生人提供的任何东西，即使是“免费的”</li>
        <li>如果有人不请自来地把手镯戴在你的手腕上，把它摘下来，马上还给你</li>
        <li>真正的佛教僧侣不会在街上卖祝福或护身符</li>
        <li>坚定地说“不，谢谢”然后走开总是有效的——他们不会跟着你的</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

    <!-- Scam 4 -->
    <h2 id="shop-tour" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
      <span class="text-4xl">🛍️</span> 4. The "My Friend Has a Shop" Tour
    </h2>

    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-900 mb-3">⚠️ How It Works</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-800 leading-relaxed">
        Same setup as the tea house scam — a friendly stranger chats you up and offers to take you to their "friend's shop" where you can get "special prices" on tea, jade, or silk. Tourist-site silver jewelry and jade stores fall into the same trap: their goods are priced far higher than shops in regular commercial districts, and authenticity can never be guaranteed.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-800 leading-relaxed mt-3">
        <strong>Where it's common:</strong> Near every major tourist attraction
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-900 mb-3">✅ How to Avoid It</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-800">
        <li>同样的规则：不要跟着陌生人去他们推荐的商店</li>
        <li>从商业区的普通商店购买纪念品，而不是从街上接近你的人那里购买</li>
        <li>如果你想要优质的茶或玉石，去信誉良好的市场。</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

    <!-- What to Do -->
    <h2 id="what-to-do" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
      <span class="text-4xl">🆘</span> What to Do If Something Happens
    </h2>

    <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <ol class="space-y-4">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="bg-red-500 text-white w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold flex-shrink-0">1</span>
          <div><strong>拨打110</strong> — police emergency line. In major cities, they can connect you to an English-speaking officer</div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="bg-red-500 text-white w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold flex-shrink-0">2</span>
          <div><strong>照相</strong> of the person, shop, or vehicle if it's safe</div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="bg-red-500 text-white w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold flex-shrink-0">3</span>
          <div><strong>致电酒店前台</strong> — they can help explain the situation to police</div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="bg-red-500 text-white w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold flex-shrink-0">4</span>
          <div><strong>不要追逐或对抗</strong> — these people know the area, you don't. Report it and move on</div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />
  </div>

  
    <!-- Sources -->
    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Sources</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <li>类型=</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Guides -->
  <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 not-prose">
    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">📚 相关指南</h3>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <a href="/zh/tips/is-china-safe/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
        <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">去中国旅行安全吗？</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">当地人的诚实回答</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/zh/tips/emergency-numbers/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
        <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">紧急电话号码和该怎么办</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">在需要之前先保存这些</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/zh/payment/payment-guide/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
        <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">如何在中国付款</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">支付宝、微信支付以及一切与金钱有关的东西</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/zh/transport/didi/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
        <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">如何在中国使用滴滴</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">中国的优步——安全又便宜</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
</Layout>